.TH MXFS_ADMIN 8 "2026-09-22" "MXFS 0.89" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
mxfs_admin \- show and change MXFS filesystem parameters
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mxfs_admin
.RB [ \-liuV ]
.RB [ \-L
.IR label ]
.RB [ \-c
.IR name ]
.RB [ \-O
.BR dirshard ]
.I device
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mxfs_admin
is the MXFS counterpart of
.BR xfs_admin (8).
The stock XFS tools read the wrong sectors on an MXFS device, because the
XFS superblock sits behind the MXFS envelope; use this tool instead.
.PP
The print options only read, and work while the filesystem is mounted.
Every change is refused unless the tool can prove that no node can write
the device:
.IP \(bu 3
the device opens exclusively on this host (not mounted here);
.IP \(bu 3
no node's heartbeat record on the device advances across a 10 second
recheck (not mounted anywhere);
.IP \(bu 3
the LUN reports no SCSI persistent-reservation registrant (nothing can
write it).  A block device that does not support persistent reservations
cannot be proven exclusive, and the change is refused.
.PP
Unmount the filesystem on every node, then run the change once from any
node that sees the device.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-l
Print the filesystem label.
.TP
.BI \-L " label"
Set the label, at most 12 bytes.  It is written to every allocation
group's superblock, each with its checksum recomputed, as
.B xfs_db
does.
.B \-\-
clears it.
.TP
.B \-u
Print the filesystem UUID.
.TP
.BI \-c " name"
Set the cluster name.  Every mount must then pass
.BI \-o " cluster=" name\fR;
see
.BR mxfs (5).
A name is 1\(en63 characters of
.BR A\-Z\ a\-z\ 0\-9\ .\ _\ \- .
.B \-c \(dq\(dq
clears it.  Use this to move a filesystem, data and all, to another
cluster.
.TP
.B \-O dirshard
Make directory sharding available on this filesystem (experimental).
Creating a sharded directory also needs the module parameter
.BR dirshard_mkdir_enable=1 .
.TP
.B \-i
Print every MXFS setting: label, UUID, cluster name, format and protocol
generation, node limit, geometry, and directory sharding state.
.TP
.B \-V
Print the version and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The device could not be read, a check failed, or a change was refused.
.SH EXAMPLES
Move a filesystem to the cluster named
.BR prod :
.PP
.RS
.nf
umount /mnt/shared          # on every node
mxfs_admin \-c prod /dev/sdb
mount \-t mxfs \-o cluster=prod /dev/sdb /mnt/shared   # on every node
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mxfs (5),
.BR mkfs.mxfs (8),
.BR chk_mxfs (8),
.BR resize_mxfs (8),
.BR xfs_admin (8)
